Section B — Temporary Commercial Restriction on the Virtual-Reserve
Bonding-Curve Algorithm
================================================================

1. Protected Algorithm

   "Protected Algorithm" means only the virtual-reserve bonding-curve
   algorithm implemented in the DuoLaunch software, comprising the
   combination of:

   (a) virtual native-asset and virtual token reserves parameterized by a
       graduation threshold p, target raise R, and token supply T, including
       formulas equivalent to:

         vToken = T * p^2 / (10000 * (2p - 10000))
         vNative = R * (10000 - p) / (2p - 10000)

   (b) buy and sell pricing based on effective reserves equivalent to:

         nativeReserve = vNative + nativeRaised
         tokenReserve  = vToken - tokensSold

   (c) using those reserves and graduation parameters together to price
       trades and graduate liquidity to a constant-product pool.

   The Protected Algorithm is asset- and chain-agnostic. Replacing the
   native asset with another blockchain's native token, a wrapped token, or
   another asset, or changing names, constants, programming languages, or
   deployment chains, does not by itself place an otherwise derivative
   implementation outside this definition.

   The generic constant-product formula x*y=k, by itself, is not the
   Protected Algorithm. This Section applies only to the algorithm described
   above and its implementations, not to the repository, DuoLaunch contract,
   interfaces, constants, or other code as a whole. It does not claim
   exclusive rights in mathematical ideas or methods as such, or in
   implementations independently created without copying protectable
   expression from this Software. A change in asset, chain, naming, or
   language alone does not establish independent creation.

2. Restriction Period

   Effective Date: 2026-10-31 00:00 UTC
   Change Date:    2029-10-31 00:00 UTC

   Before the Effective Date, Section A applies to the Protected Algorithm.
   The "Restriction Period" begins on the Effective Date and ends
   immediately before the Change Date. The Change Date applies to this
   release and all versions of the Protected Algorithm distributed under
   this License. Earlier releases remain subject to the license terms
   distributed with those releases.

