   non-commercial testing, research, education, and deployment. You must
   retain this License and applicable copyright notices in copies or
   substantial portions of the Protected Algorithm.

   "Commercial purpose" means an activity primarily intended for or
   directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation. During
   the Restriction Period, you may not, without prior written permission
   from the copyright holder:

   (a) deploy or operate the Protected Algorithm or an implementation
       derived from it in a commercial product, protocol, or service; or

   (b) create, commission, distribute, offer, sell, license, or otherwise
       provide a derivative implementation for a commercial purpose.

   Commercial integration with or use of the canonical Duo contracts as a
   user or frontend/router integrator is not, by itself, deployment of a
   separate implementation of the Protected Algorithm.

